50
00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.980
He held a press conference
this morning.

51
00:03:09.064 --> 00:03:11.534
- A press conference?
- What does that mean?

52
00:03:11.608 --> 00:03:13.408
"A person of interest?"
What the fuck is that?

53
00:03:13.443 --> 00:03:15.453
Character assassination is what it is.

54
00:03:15.737 --> 00:03:17.907
- It's a tactic.
- It means nothing legally.

55
00:03:17.989 --> 00:03:19.029
Doesn't feel like nothing.

56
00:03:19.074 --> 00:03:21.552
- Feels like they're about to arrest me!
- They can't.

57
00:03:21.576 --> 00:03:24.826
They don't have enough.
So they try to put public pressure on you.

58
00:03:25.163 --> 00:03:27.213
They don't have the evidence
to call you a suspect.

59
00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:28.330
but they want you scared.

60
00:03:28.417 --> 00:03:30.019
- Well done. then.
- Maybe it's best

61
00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:32.593
- if you boys stay home from school today.
- No.

62
00:03:33.338 --> 00:03:34.838
No way. We're not doing that.

63
00:03:35.465 --> 00:03:36.925
- Clay...
- You can stay home.

64
00:03:37.259 --> 00:03:40.139
No. of course not.
I've got your back. That's what we do.

65
00:03:43.515 --> 00:03:45.675
Let's get a coffee on the way and talk.

66
00:03:49.354 --> 00:03:51.314
<i>And then the bad news gets worse.</i>

67
00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:55.069
<i>And it feels like the world is closing in.</i>

68
00:03:57.529 --> 00:03:58.529
Taken?

69
00:04:00.198 --> 00:04:02.318
- Knock yourself out.
- Yeah. I should hope not.

70
00:04:02.826 --> 00:04:05.196
